WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.670
A questionnaire slides across the desk.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.520
Do you like going out a lot?

3
00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.620
Do you often feel fed up?

4
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.720
Your answers become scores on three dials.

5
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.130
One psychologist claimed that the right
combination of scores marks out a criminal

6
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.420
personality.

7
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:19.720
So could a personality test really
predict who ends up in court?

8
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.290
In this mission, you'll see how Eysenck
measured personality with a questionnaire,

9
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.650
scoring people along dimensions.

10
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.390
You'll find out which scores
he linked to offending,

11
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.650
and why he blamed the nervous
system we are born with.

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.910
Then you'll weigh up the evidence.

13
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.970
Your mission: decide whether a personality
test could predict who ends up in court.
